# Dual fuzz harnesses (AFL++ and ClusterFuzzLite)

When adding or renaming a fuzz target, keep **both** engines in sync (same
basename, e.g. `fuzz_pyproject_toml`):

- **AFL++ (NFR-020):** `tests/fuzz/fuzz_targets/`, `tests/fuzz/Cargo.toml`
  `[[bin]]`, corpus under `tests/fuzz/corpus/<format>/`, and
  `scripts/fuzz-targets.map` (map sync is manual; not covered by
  `check-fuzz-target-parity`)
- **cargo-fuzz / CFL:** `fuzz/fuzz_targets/<name>.rs` (no `catch_unwind`),
  `[[bin]]` in `fuzz/Cargo.toml`, corpus under `fuzz/corpus/<name>/`

After harness or `Cargo.toml` edits run `make check-fuzz-target-parity`. Do not
treat `fuzz/**/*.rs` as a root-workspace crate for `make clippy` /
`make cargo-test` (rustfmt hook still formats harness `.rs` files).
ClusterFuzzLite `build.sh` needs nightly via `RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN` (root
`rust-toolchain.toml` pins stable). See CONTRIBUTING "Fuzz testing".
